server: free_async_queue() drops the queue's reference to an async once

free_async_queue() called async_terminate() with the async still on the
queue. When no APC can be queued (the async's process is gone, as at
the wineserver's exit), async_terminate() sets the result at once, and
async_set_result() removes a queued async from its queue and drops the
queue's reference; free_async_queue() then dropped it again. On Haiku this
happened at every wineserver exit (a named pipe server's listen queue):
"server/object.c:566:release_object: obj->refcount", Abort -- before the
registry was saved, so a value written less than the save period before
the exit was lost (reg add, then the server's exit: the value is gone).

The async now leaves the queue before it is terminated.

--- a/server/async.c
+++ b/server/async.c
@@ -277,8 +277,12 @@
     {
         if (!async->completion) async->completion = fd_get_completion( async->fd, &async->comp_key );
         async->fd = NULL;
-        async_terminate( async, STATUS_HANDLES_CLOSED );
+        /* off the queue before it terminates: when no APC can be queued (the process is gone),
+         * async_terminate() sets the result at once, and async_set_result() would drop the queue's
+         * reference itself, which is dropped below */
+        list_remove( &async->queue_entry );
         async->queue = NULL;
+        async_terminate( async, STATUS_HANDLES_CLOSED );
         release_object( &async->obj );
     }
 }
